20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [247 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [288 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [305 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [387 2 "// __module__, __qualname__, __doc__"] [407 32 "// not when __slots__ names __doc__ (typing's _SpecialForm): the slot's descriptor is it"] [409 2 "// __new__ a staticmethod, __init_subclass__ and __class_getitem__ classmethods"] [418 2 "// __slots__"] [422 20 "// a class without __slots__ gives its instances a __dict__"] [483 2 "// __classcell__, __classdictcell__"] [500 2 "// __eq__ without __hash__ makes the class unhashable"] [508 2 "// __set_name__"] [520 2 "// __init_subclass__"] [535 1 "// checkLayouts refuses bases whose instance layouts conflict."] [546 1 "// bestBase is best_base: the base whose solid base is the most derived."] [564 1 "// c3MRO is the C3 linearization of t over its bases (mro_internal's mro_implementation)."] [623 1 "// mangle is _Py_Mangle: __x in class C is _C__x."] [646 1 "// ---- object.__new__, object.__init__ ----"] [648 1 "// overrides is a heap class of t's MRO defining name, or, for __new__, t's built-in solid base not"] [649 1 "// object (a built-in type's inherited slot cannot be told from its own: Go's functions do not compare)."] [660 4 "// a static type's tp_name is its module's and its name (select.poll)"] [706 25 "// its __del__ at its death (finalize.go, queue 218)"] [725 2 "// The data model's slots of object and type (REQUEST to PY5b: leave these to class.go)."] [738 1 "// ---- the slots of a class (fixup_slot_dispatchers, update_slot) ----"] [744 1 "// pyDefined is name defined by a heap class of t's MRO (a Python method), and its value."] [753 1 "// fixupSlots fills t's slots: the built-in solid base's (unwrapping a built-in subclass's value),"] [754 1 "// then a dispatcher for each special method a class of the MRO defines. Rerun on a class's"] [755 1 "// special attribute's assignment, for it and its subclasses."] [779 4 "// dict's subscript sees the subclass's instance (its __missing__; dict's accessors take the"] [780 4 "// instance through BuiltinValueHook): PY5e, part 2b"] [904 4 "// slot_tp_call's _Py_EnterRecursiveCall (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's"] [905 4 "// test_recursive_call, A.__call__ = A(), overflowed Go's stack)"] [1074 1 "// reprOfInstance are the built-in types whose repr names the instance's own type (_PyType_Name(Py_TYPE(self)):"] [1075 1 "// deque's, defaultdict's): their subclasses' instances reach the Repr slot as they are, not unwrapped (PY7: a"] [1076 1 "// subclass's repr named the base)."] [1079 1 "// unwrapSlots makes a built-in base's slots work on its subclass's instances: each argument that is"] [1080 1 "// such an instance replaced by its value, and the base's __new__'s value wrapped in the instance."] [1148 1 "// wrapNew is a built-in __new__ called for a class deriving from it: its value in an instance."] [1157 1 "// wrapInstance is the instance of the heap class t that keeps the built-in value v (wrapNew's), tracked when t"] [1158 1 "// defines __del__ (queue 218)."] [1172 26 "// socket.socket's: sock_finalize at its death"] [1177 1 "// callSpecial calls o's special method name (looked up on its type, as CPython's lookup_maybe_method)."] [1183 2 "// the C level's recursion check (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_repr_as_str,"] [1184 2 "// __repr__ = __str__ through built-in slot wrappers, overflowed Go's stack)"] [1199 1 "// callSpecialOr is callSpecial, NotImplemented when o's type has no such method."] [1208 1 "// CallSpecial calls o's special method name, found reports whether o's type has it (for the"] [1209 1 "// built-ins with no slot: __abs__, __divmod__, __round__, __format__, __reversed__ ...)."] [1219 1 "// asIndex is operator.index(o)."] [1242 1 "// objectRichCompare is object's __eq__ (identity), __ne__ (__eq__ inverted), the rest NotImplemented."] [1268 1 "// updateSubclassSlots refills the slots of t and its subclasses after a special attribute changed"] [1269 1 "// (update_slot over the subclasses: the type version tags' invalidation)."] [1280 1 "// IsSubclass is issubclass(c, cls) with __subclasscheck__; IsInstanceOf isinstance(o, cls) with"] [1281 1 "// __instancecheck__ (PyObject_IsInstance, PyObject_IsSubclass)."] [1287 3 "// \"Not a general sequence -- that opens up the road to recursion and stack overflow\" (PY7: the C"] [1288 3 "// level's check, test_isinstance's test_isinstance_recursion_limit overflowed Go's stack)"] [1341 58 "// object_issubclass's (PY7)"] [1380 1 "// checkClass is check_class: o's __bases__ a tuple, else the TypeError msg; an error other than AttributeError"] [1381 1 "// getting it raised as it is (PY7: it became the TypeError)."] [1393 1 "// abstractIsSubclass is abstract_issubclass: c's __bases__ walked, an error other than AttributeError raised"] [1394 1 "// (PY7: it was dropped), the C level's check before each recursion (test_isinstance's"] [1395 1 "// test_infinite_recursion_via_bases_tuple and test_infinite_cycle_in_bases overflowed Go's stack)."] [1430 1 "// posArgs checks a built-in's positional argument count, CPython's messages."] [1448 1 "// ---- object's pickling protocol (typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex__, reduce_newobj, object_getstate) ----"] [1450 1 "// importModule is __import__(name) through the interpreter's builtins (PY5e's import system)."] [1459 1 "// importErrorType is ImportError when the runtime has it, else RuntimeError."] [1475 1 "// objectGetState is object.__getstate__: the instance's __dict__ (None when empty), with its"] [1476 1 "// __slots__' values as a second dictionary."] [1569 3 "// typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex___impl: a __reduce__ overriding object's, a built-in type's too"] [1595 1 "// BuiltinValue is the built-in value an instance of 